/*!
    \page troubleshooting.html
    \title Troubleshooting
    \previouspage Project Structure
    \nextpage About and Version Information

    This chapter lists the most common problems and how to diagnose them. The first stop
    for any issue is the \b{log panel} and the \b{application log file}, whose folder can
    be opened from the UI.

    \section1 Cannot connect to a server

    \list
        \li \b{Wrong URL or unreachable host.} Confirm the endpoint URL
            (\c {opc.tcp://host:port}) and that the server is running and reachable.
        \li \b{Security policy mismatch.} The client's selected security policy must be
            one the server offers. Try \e None first to isolate a security problem.
        \li \b{Certificate not trusted.} With signing/encryption, the two sides must
            trust each other's certificates. Check the PKI store (see \l {Configuration}).
        \li \b{Identity rejected.} Anonymous access may be disabled, or the
            username/password may be wrong.
    \endlist

    \section1 Values do not update

    \list
        \li Confirm the variable is actually \e subscribed (not just read once).
        \li Check the variable's access level — some nodes are read-only.
        \li For a designed server, confirm the variable has a \e simulation if you expect
            it to change on its own (see \l {OPC UA Server}).
    \endlist

    \section1 The local server does not start

    \list
        \li \b{Runtime not found.} The headless \b OpcUaServerRuntime executable must sit
            next to the application; a broken deployment is the usual cause.
        \li \b{Port already in use.} Another server may hold the configured port; change
            the endpoint port.
        \li \b{Invalid project.} The validator reports problems (for example a node that
            references a namespace the project does not declare) before the server starts.
        \li \b{Crash on start.} The controller reports a crash and the runtime's output is
            captured in the log; restart or kill and retry.
    \endlist

    \section1 Configuration or data problems

    \list
        \li \b{Settings not persisting.} Confirm whether the app is running installed or
            portable and that the writable data location is accessible (see
            \l {Configuration}).
        \li \b{Corrupt project file.} Projects are written atomically, but an
            externally edited \c .uaproj / \c .uaserver may fail to load; the loader
            reports a typed error.
    \endlist

    \section1 Collecting diagnostics

    When reporting a problem, include the application version (see
    \l {About and Version Information}) and the relevant section of the log file.
*/
